module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.type_parameter_kind_deferral_never_collected

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// A DEFERRED JUDGMENT THAT WAS NEVER COLLECTED, AND SHIPPED AS IF IT WERE A VERDICT. v2's kinded-slot
// wall carried an arm that admitted ANY type argument merely because it was a bound type parameter.
// The arm was introduced as a DECLARED DEFERRAL -- the binder was to collect the forwarded parameter's
// kind later and the arm was then to become a judgment -- and the collector never arrived, so a
// temporary became permanent behaviour with no owner and no observation. HARM: a parameter forwarded
// into a slot declared with a kind passed the slot whether it was declared with that kind, with a
// different kind, or with no kind at all, so "this position was kind-checked" was false for every
// forwarded parameter in the corpus while the wall's own name and type said otherwise.
data type_parameter_kind_deferral_never_collected: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "type_parameter_kind_deferral_never_collected" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "THE DEFERRAL, AND WHAT IT FAILED TO PAY. v2.compiler.resolve resolve_kind_inhabitance answered an argument that resolves to a bound type parameter with the one arm v2.std.type_binder KindInhabitance reserves for exactly that case, and v2.std.type_binder type_application_conformance folds that arm to CONFORMANCE -- an admit. Its documentation framed the missing judgment as pending, to be collected by the binder. Nothing in the tree ever collected it: the arm had no path to a judgment and no diagnostic named its absence, so the wall could not distinguish 'deferred' from 'verified'.",

    "PROVENANCE, from git log -S over the arm. a21a9014dae (#13038) introduced it as the declared deferral. f10cf27fc28 (#13293) reverted that change. 86cbb993b35 (#13309) re-landed it. The re-land carried the arm and its framing forward and still carried no collector, which is the failure this row names: the revert-and-reland cycle moved the deferral without ever paying it, and no claim or census observed the difference between the three states.",

    "WHY A NAMED, TYPED, DOCUMENTED ARM IS STILL NOT A WALL. The arm was reachable by ordinary code -- a generic forwarding one of its own parameters into a kinded slot is routine -- so this was not a dead branch waiting for an unusual input. It was live, and it decided nothing. A reader inspecting the wall saw a kinded-slot check with a type-parameter case handled and a named diagnostic class (TypeApplicationKindNotInhabited) sitting beside it; the class was real and reachable for a NAMED non-inhabitant, which is precisely what made the parameter case look covered. The guarantee was false only where the argument was a parameter, which is where forwarding puts it.",

    "WHAT CLOSED IT, and the rule that made the closure admissible. The arm now routes to a judgment over declarations: the parameter's own declared kind, read through the index at the declaration that binds it, compared against the kind the position asks for -- which the wall had already resolved from the APPLIED declaration. No identity-to-spelling fallback and no ambient admission (the 2026-10-15 ruling): a parameter declared without a kind, or with another kind, refuses, because a name that stands for an unknown set of inhabitants establishes nothing about them. The arm itself is retained and left unproduced rather than deleted, because removing it reaches the emitter's enum mirror and the machine-width literal roster frontier -- a different change from closing a widen, and this row is about the widen.",

    "THE ASYMMETRY THIS ROW RECORDS FOR THE OTHER FRONT END. The same position in v1 (v1.compiler.infer_resolve type_arg_kind_inhabitance, its two unconditional admits) is NOT closed by this row's fix and cannot be closed there: the v1 wall is handed the argument as a de-identified leaf, so no predicate at that site can be grounded. That is its own class with its own measurement, recorded in kind_wall_receives_a_de_identified_type_argument. Filing them together would hide the difference that matters: v2's arm could judge and did not; v1's cannot judge yet, and the repair belongs above it."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.resolve", decl_name: "resolve_kind_inhabitance", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.type_binder", decl_name: "type_application_conformance", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.type_binder", decl_name: "KindInhabitance", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ]
}
